---
// Explanatory content, best practices, presets, and FAQ for UTM Builder
---

<article class="w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto pt-14 sm:pt-16 mt-14 sm:mt-16 border-t border-[var(--border-hairline)] space-y-12 text-[var(--text-primary)]">
  <!-- Introduction & Overview -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)] leading-snug">
      What is the UTM Builder and Why Clean URL Generation Matters
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
      The UTM Builder is a specialized campaign URL generator that constructs clean, standards-compliant tracking links for digital marketing campaigns. Instead of manually editing URL query strings—which frequently introduces syntax errors, broken delimiters, and malformed encoding—the UTM Builder provides a guided, real-time interface that automatically formats, validates, and encodes every parameter.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
      Proper campaign tracking is the backbone of marketing attribution. When tracking tags are formulated with precision, analytics tools such as Google Analytics 4 (GA4), Mixpanel, and Adobe Analytics can cleanly attribute every session, purchase, and lead back to the exact ad creative, campaign theme, and marketing channel that produced it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Parameter Blueprint Guide -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">
      The 5 Core UTM Parameters Blueprint
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
      A complete tracking URL combines your destination address with standardized query parameters:
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/30 space-y-1.5">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="font-mono text-[var(--accent)] font-medium text-xs">1. Destination URL</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-emerald-400 font-sans uppercase font-medium">Required</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          The webpage where visitors arrive after clicking your link (e.g., <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">https://example.com/summer-sale</code>). Can include existing query parameters or sub-paths.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/30 space-y-1.5">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="font-mono text-[var(--accent)] font-medium text-xs">2. utm_source</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-emerald-400 font-sans uppercase font-medium">Required</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          The referrer or platform delivering the traffic (e.g., <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">google</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">facebook</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">linkedin</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">customerio</code>).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/30 space-y-1.5">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="font-mono text-[var(--accent)] font-medium text-xs">3. utm_medium</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-emerald-400 font-sans uppercase font-medium">Required</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          The marketing mechanism or delivery medium. Must match GA4 Default Channel Grouping rules (e.g., <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">cpc</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">email</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">paid_social</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">referral</code>).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/30 space-y-1.5">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="font-mono text-[var(--accent)] font-medium text-xs">4. utm_campaign</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-emerald-400 font-sans uppercase font-medium">Required</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          The strategic name, promotion, or campaign ID (e.g., <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">spring_clearance</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">brand_awareness_2026</code>).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/30 space-y-1.5">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="font-mono text-[var(--text-secondary)] font-medium text-xs">5. utm_term &amp; utm_content</span>
          <span class="text-[10px] text-[var(--text-muted)] font-sans uppercase">Optional</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">utm_term</code> records targeted keywords or audiences, while <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">utm_content</code> differentiates ad creatives, button designs, or link positions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Step by step usage -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">
      How to Build Campaign Links Step-by-Step
    </h2>
    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3.5 py-2">
        <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--bg-subtle)] text-[var(--text-primary)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] font-medium flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 text-xs">1</span>
        <div>
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-medium">Enter Destination URL:</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">Specify the exact landing page. If you omit the protocol, the builder automatically maintains standard web protocol conventions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3.5 py-2">
        <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--bg-subtle)] text-[var(--text-primary)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] font-medium flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 text-xs">2</span>
        <div>
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-medium">Apply a Preset or Enter Custom Tags:</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">Choose a pre-configured channel preset (Google Ads, Meta Ads, Email, LinkedIn) or input custom source, medium, and campaign identifiers.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3.5 py-2">
        <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--bg-subtle)] text-[var(--text-primary)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] font-medium flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 text-xs">3</span>
        <div>
          <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-medium">Copy the Encoded Campaign Link:</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-0.5 leading-relaxed">The tool automatically escapes special characters, encodes spaces as <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">%20</code>, and generates an optimized URL ready for deployment.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Preset Reference Table -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">
      Recommended Source &amp; Medium Combinations for GA4
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
      Google Analytics 4 uses rigid rules to categorize sessions into Default Channel Groups. Following these combinations prevents your traffic from falling into Unassigned:
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)]">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/40 text-[var(--text-muted)] text-[11px] font-mono">
            <th class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">Channel</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">utm_source</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">utm_medium</th>
            <th class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">GA4 Channel Group</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--border-hairline)] text-xs">
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Google Search Ads</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">google</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">cpc</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-emerald-400">Paid Search</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Meta (Facebook/IG) Ads</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">facebook / instagram</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">cpc / paid_social</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-emerald-400">Paid Social</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Email Newsletter</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">newsletter</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">email</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-emerald-400">Email</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">LinkedIn Organic Posts</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">linkedin</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">social</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-emerald-400">Organic Social</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">Affiliate Partner</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">[partner_name]</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono text-[var(--accent)]">affiliate</td>
            <td class="py-2.5 px-4 text-emerald-400">Affiliates</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 Critical Rules -->
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">
      5 Critical URL Building Guidelines
    </h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 text-sm">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/20 space-y-1.5">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-xs text-[var(--text-primary)]">1. Encode Spaces with %20</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          While some legacy systems use <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">+</code> for spaces, modern web standards and RFC 3986 recommend <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">%20</code> to avoid ambiguity with literal plus symbols.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/20 space-y-1.5">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-xs text-[var(--text-primary)]">2. Preserve Existing Query Keys</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          If your destination URL already contains parameters (e.g. <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">?variant=12</code>), the builder attaches UTM tags using ampersands (<code class="font-mono text-[11px]">&amp;</code>) automatically.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/20 space-y-1.5">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-xs text-[var(--text-primary)]">3. Keep Hash Fragments at the End</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Page anchors like <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">#pricing</code> must remain at the very end of the URL. Placing query parameters after the hash prevents servers from reading them.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-[var(--border-hairline)] bg-[var(--bg-subtle)]/20 space-y-1.5">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-xs text-[var(--text-primary)]">4. Never Store Personally Identifiable Data</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Do not include customer email addresses, account IDs, or phone numbers in UTM fields. Doing so violates privacy laws (GDPR, CCPA) and analytics terms.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tool FAQ Section — clean divider-based accordion -->
  <section class="space-y-6 pt-4" id="faq">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h2 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">
        Frequently Asked Questions About the UTM Builder
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        Common questions on creating, encoding, and deploying UTM campaign links.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="divide-y divide-[var(--border-hairline)] border-y border-[var(--border-hairline)]">
      <details class="group py-4 transition-colors [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-medium text-sm text-[var(--text-primary)] select-none">
          <span>What happens if my destination URL already has query parameters?</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[var(--text-muted)] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.75" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed pr-6">
          The UTM Builder intelligently detects existing query parameters (such as <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">?ref=partner</code> or <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">?id=123</code>) and seamlessly appends UTM tags with ampersands (<code class="font-mono text-[11px]">&amp;</code>). It never adds duplicate question marks, preserving your URL's technical integrity.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4 transition-colors [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-medium text-sm text-[var(--text-primary)] select-none">
          <span>Why does the builder use %20 instead of + for spaces?</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[var(--text-muted)] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.75" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed pr-6">
          Standard RFC 3986 specifies that spaces in URLs are encoded as <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">%20</code>. While HTML form data historically used plus signs (<code class="font-mono text-[11px]">+</code>), many modern JavaScript frameworks, web routers, and analytics APIs parse <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">+</code> literally rather than as a space, causing attribution discrepancies.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4 transition-colors [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-medium text-sm text-[var(--text-primary)] select-none">
          <span>Which UTM parameters are strictly required for GA4?</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[var(--text-muted)] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.75" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed pr-6">
          Technically, any single parameter will be processed, but best practice and GA4 attribution modeling require at least <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-medium">utm_source</strong>, <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-medium">utm_medium</strong>, and <strong class="text-[var(--text-primary)] font-medium">utm_campaign</strong>. Without these three core dimensions, sessions cannot be grouped into primary acquisition channels accurately.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4 transition-colors [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-medium text-sm text-[var(--text-primary)] select-none">
          <span>Does UTMVerify store or log the URLs I build?</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[var(--text-muted)] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.75" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed pr-6">
          No. UTMVerify runs completely client-side in your web browser. Neither your destination landing pages nor your UTM tags are transmitted to our servers, saved in a database, or tracked. Your campaign strategy remains 100% confidential.
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4 transition-colors [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-medium text-sm text-[var(--text-primary)] select-none">
          <span>When should I use Bulk UTM Builder instead of this single builder?</span>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[var(--text-muted)] group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.75" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed pr-6">
          Use the UTM Builder for individual links, ad creatives, or one-off social posts. If you are planning an omni-channel launch requiring 5, 10, or 50+ URLs across multiple ad sets and newsletters, use the <a href="./bulk-utm-builder" class="text-[var(--accent)] hover:underline font-medium">Bulk UTM Builder</a> to configure and export links in a spreadsheet matrix.
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>

<!-- Structured Data for FAQ -->
